  "notes": "Professional phase only: catalog Semesters 5-9 of the BSN (70 credits). The catalog's 50 credits of required general education & science courses (BIO 189, BIO 201, BIO 202, BIO 205, CHM 130, ENG 101, ENG 102, PSC 101*, HCR 230, HCR 240, MAT 151, NTR 241, PSY 101, PSY 230, PSY 240; *not applicable in Colorado) are completed in semesters 1-4 or via transfer; the catalog prints them as a flat block with no semester assignment, so they are documented here rather than seeded as invented semesters. Per catalog p.17, students who complete the general education curriculum (grade/GPA criteria) progress into the core nursing courses beginning in semester five. Program is identical across all Arizona College of Nursing campuses: one institution-wide 2026 catalog governs every campus; the only state-specific schedule variations are Colorado (higher practicum credits: 73-core subtotal) and California (separate contact-hour table plus LVN 30-unit option). Tampa FL, Tempe AZ, and Tucson AZ are unaffected, so the 70-credit core applies to all three. Prereq note: the catalog lists 'Admission to Core Nursing Program' (not a course code) as the prerequisite for Semester 5 courses and NUR 337; it is documented here, not as a machine prereq. Titles transcribed from the catalog's SCHEDULE OF COURSES table; the description pages print 'Leader in Quality & Patient Safety II/IV' where the schedule table prints 'Leader in Quality Care & Patient Safety II/IV' -- the schedule table wording is used. Per-semester subtotals (13/15/15/13/14) reconcile exactly with the catalog's printed subtotals; total_credits (70) matches the catalog's NURSING CORE COURSES SUBTOTAL and the grand total 120 (50 gen-ed + 70 core).",
